WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.920
Mexico City, 1989.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.120
To clean up the air,

3
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.080
the city bans most cars from
driving one weekday a week.

4
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.120
Your day off the road depends on the last

5
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.920
digit of your number plate.

6
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.240
Fewer cars, cleaner air.

7
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.620
That was the plan.

8
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:20.030
But a 2008 study found no
evidence that the air got cleaner.

9
00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.440
When a government steps
in to fix a market,

10
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.110
how can it end up making things worse?

11
00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.280
In this mission, you'll set
a pollution tax yourself

12
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.900
and find the point where it
starts doing more harm than good.

13
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.590
Then you'll see how a
farm policy built butter

14
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.780
mountains and wine lakes.

15
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.380
Your mission: find out when
stepping in makes things worse,

16
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.330
and how to tell.
